%description:

Tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass:dctcp-reduction -- an ECE reduces the window by alpha/2, and the threshold is 3/4 of the flight.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "the NED type of the algorithm of each connection"; the comment of
each algorithm module names its behavior. The claim of DcTcp (RFC 8257 section 3.3.9): the window shrinks in proportion
to the fraction of marked bytes, cwnd * (1 - alpha / 2), and not by half.

The class dctcp-reduction: DcTcp::processEce() reduces the window once in each window of data
that has marks, and sets the threshold to 3/4 of min(cwnd, snd_wnd). This facet comes from the coverage gap loop: no test reached the code of this part. This test separates
"dctcp" from the classic algorithms, which halve the window, and from TcpCubic, whose
threshold is 0.7 of the window.

Host under test: host1, with DcTcp; host1 sends 100000 bytes at 0.2 s, and the tap marks the
15th data segment CE; host1 uses classic ECN (tcpEcnMode "rfc3168", a precondition), and host2
answers it (passive, the default). Alpha starts at 0, so one marked segment gives a small alpha. Observation:
level 2, the first threshold after the mark is between 0.73 and 0.76 of the largest window
before it.

%# parameter: Tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass
%# class: dctcp-reduction
%# value: "DcTcp"
%# key: *.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpAlgorithmClassDcTcpReduction")
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host1").filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 1 + 14 * 1448 && ipv4.totalLengthField > 100B").nth(1)
                     .set("ipv4.ecn", "3")
                     .describe("the 15th data segment of host1: mark it CE"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .meanwhile(anyNumberOfTimes(on("host1.tcp").signal("cwnd")
                                        .captureMax("cwndBefore", "value")
                                        .within(4.0)))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("ssthresh")
                  .filterValueAtMost(1e8)
                  .first()
                  .assertEvent([](const MatchContext& context) {
                      double ratio = context.event.value / context.get("cwndBefore").doubleValue();
                      return ratio >= 0.73 && ratio <= 0.76;
                  })
                  .describe("the threshold at the reaction to the ECE, 3/4 of the flight")
                  .within(1.5));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpAlgorithmClassDcTcpReduction compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass = "DcTcp"    # the parameter under test
*.linkDelay = 10ms
*.host1.tcp.tcpEcnMode = "rfc3168"
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 100000B
*.host1.tcp.sackSupport = false
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpAlgorithmClassDcTcpReduction: PASS
